---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import { APPS } from '../../data/apps';
import { site } from '../../content';
const title = 'Shopify SMS apps and retention tools: selection guide';
const desc = 'Browse 21 app reviews and compare SMS delivery, email automation, capture and migration requirements without unsupported rankings.';
const path = '/apps';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-14 md:py-20">
    <header class="max-w-4xl">
      <p class="badge">21 app reviews · selection guide</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Shopify SMS apps and retention tools</h1>
      <p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">Choose the job before choosing the app. Sending texts, collecting subscribers and building post-purchase email are different requirements. This directory includes SMS platforms and adjacent tools; inclusion does not mean that every product sends SMS or replaces your existing email service.</p>
      <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8">The catalog order is navigation, not a performance ranking. We have not run comparative store tests or established a universal winner. Use the workflow checks below to narrow a shortlist, then follow the individual reviews and comparisons for the relevant decision.</p>
    </header>
    <article class="prose-shopify mt-12 max-w-4xl">
      <h2>Start with what already works</h2>
      <p>Inventory Shopify automations and third-party senders before adding another one. Shopify now calls its native app Shopify Messaging and documents email, SMS and WhatsApp marketing automations. Its recovery templates distinguish product browse, cart and checkout. Native capability is a real starting point, although the channels and configuration available to your account need checking.</p>
      <p>For each missing journey, write the trigger, required customer identity, product information, destination, exclusions and person responsible. A product-view event without an identified subscriber is a different problem from a checkout email skipped after purchase. Changing vendors will not repair missing identity or an intentionally excluded recipient.</p>
      <h2>Four different shortlist decisions</h2>
      <table class="data-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Job</th><th>Evidence to request</th><th>Useful acceptance example</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>SMS delivery and replies</td><td>Supported countries, sender setup, reply routing and itemized message charges</td><td>A product question reaches the assigned inbox; an opt-out stops the next eligible marketing step.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Email and SMS coordination</td><td>Event mapping, channel eligibility and cancellation behavior</td><td>A completed order removes the shopper from obsolete cart recovery while the intended receipt still sends.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Subscriber capture</td><td>Form behavior, destination fields and separate channel permission records</td><td>A new form submission reaches the right audience once, with its collection source intact.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Guided operation</td><td>Actual service scope, approval responsibilities and handover documentation</td><td>Your regular operator can change an exclusion and explain who handles a failed integration.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <h2>Documented starting points, without a winner</h2>
      <p>Postscript currently presents SMS, RCS and email on its platform site. Treating it categorically as SMS-only would miss its advertised scope; request an email demonstration if consolidation matters. Its marketing does not establish that every channel or feature is available under your proposed contract.</p>
      <p>Omnisend documents Shopify customer, product and order sync for targeted email and SMS. That makes it a relevant candidate for a shared commerce workspace. Ask how a changed order and a withdrawal reach a waiting automation rather than assuming the initial import proves ongoing synchronization.</p>
      <p>Sequenzy documents campaigns, automation, transactional email, API and MCP access, along with Shopify integration and SMS/MMS in its feature directory. Agent access can be useful when an operator wants to inspect and edit email operations through tools. Evaluate approval controls and the actual Shopify event path; neither agent access nor generated copy proves incremental revenue or faster implementation.</p>
      <p>Klaviyo publishes a Shopify integration setup guide. If it is on your shortlist, use that guide to trace the events your proposed flow needs and ask the intended operator to maintain a sample branch. Avoid choosing on a generic “data depth” label without naming the fields and decisions involved.</p>
      <h2>Full catalog</h2>
      <p>All 21 review destinations remain available below. Some cover adjacent email, capture or legacy migration decisions. Read the current supplier documentation for the specific product you intend to buy; a legacy review URL is not proof of current availability.</p>
    </article>
    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      {APPS.map((app) => (
        <a class="card" href={`/apps/${app.slug}`}><h2 class="text-xl font-black">{app.name}</h2><p class="mt-3">Read the app-specific workflow and integration discussion →</p></a>
      ))}
    </div>
    <article class="prose-shopify mt-12 max-w-4xl">
      <h2>Proposed trial: a furniture cart and a financing question</h2>
      <p>For a hypothetical $840 furniture cart, separate the shopper’s question about financing from the promotional reminder. Check whether the selected sender can route a reply to someone who can answer it, preserve the correct cart link and cancel the reminder after purchase. Use an unavailable variant and a purchase made while the message is waiting as counterexamples.</p>
      <p>Do not infer SMS permission from an unopened email. Confirm the applicable channel, purpose and destination requirements and preserve the collection evidence. Choose a contact policy based on the journey and customer expectations instead of a universal twenty-four-hour channel gap. These are proposed checks, not an observed store implementation.</p>
      <h2>Proposed trial: a vinyl release versus pet replenishment</h2>
      <p>A vinyl release needs accurate stock and launch timing. Ask what happens when a linked pressing sells out while a message waits. A pet subscription needs renewal and cancellation state: a generic interval since purchase may remind someone whose next shipment is already scheduled. These scenarios expose different data needs; the same “automation” feature label does not answer both.</p>
      <p>For a capture experiment, count eligible visitors and valid subscribers separately. For a recovery experiment, compare randomized eligible groups when volume permits, report uncertainty, and reconcile refunds and discounts. Clicks and attributed orders are useful diagnostics but do not by themselves establish additional orders.</p>
      <h2>Price the actual journey</h2>
      <p>Request platform fees, billable profiles or contacts, email volume, SMS segments, destination and carrier charges, sender registration, support and implementation costs. Include a normal month and a peak month. A long message or a destination change can alter the SMS estimate even when the recipient count stays the same.</p>
      <p>Illustrative arithmetic: 20 additional fulfilled orders contributing $30 each before an extra $8 incentive produce $440 after those incentives. If the trial adds $120 in messaging and platform costs, contribution is $320 before additional labor. That calculation depends on orders being incremental; substituting 20 attributed orders would not establish the same result.</p>
      <h2>Cut over a workflow, not every notification</h2>
      <p>List existing enrollment points and waiting queues. Choose whether old contacts finish in the old sender or are cancelled and deliberately enrolled in the replacement. Test purchase exits and withdrawal propagation before enabling new enrollment. Retain a rollback plan that prevents replaying already completed steps.</p>
      <p>Keep transactional receipts and service notifications assigned explicitly. A marketing migration need not move them. Review delivery failures, replies and opt-outs after launch at a cadence appropriate to send volume, and investigate changes by journey instead of imposing one fixed operating schedule on every store.</p>
      <h2>Continue with the decision you actually need</h2>
      <p><a class="link" href="/compare">Pair comparisons</a> help when two products remain. The <a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">cart recovery guide</a> focuses on recovery execution; <a class="link" href="/for">store-type guides</a> add catalog and purchase-cycle context. If the question is whether to replace native email, use the <a class="link" href="/alternatives/shopify-email-alternative">Shopify Email alternatives guide</a>.</p>
      <h2>Primary sources and limits</h2>
      <p>Documentation checked November 25, 2026. Supplier descriptions establish advertised scope, not comparative performance. The examples above are proposed evaluations and illustrative arithmetic.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a class="link" href="https://help.shopify.com/en/manual/promoting-marketing/create-marketing/shopify-messaging/marketing-automations">Shopify Messaging automations</a></li>
        <li><a class="link" href="https://postscript.io/">Postscript platform channels</a></li>
        <li><a class="link" href="https://support.omnisend.com/en/articles/3175406-connect-your-shopify-store-to-omnisend">Omnisend Shopify sync</a></li>
        <li><a class="link" href="https://www.sequenzy.com/features">Sequenzy feature directory</a></li>
        <li><a class="link" href="https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/115005080407">Klaviyo Shopify setup</a></li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
